---
import DocsLayout from '@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { DocsTable } from '@/molecules/DocComponents/DocComponents';

const CHANNELS = [
  ['Nexus → Manager', 'Workspace runtime access token', 'Worker requests, status, heartbeats, and GitHub credential requests'],
  ['Manager → Coder', 'Platform operator credential', 'Template publication and workspace creation or lifecycle'],
  ['Runtime → Redis', 'Tenant Redis ACL credential', 'Ticket state, worker slots, heartbeats, A2A evidence'],
  ['Coder → Manager → Nexus', 'Global then tenant hook JWT', 'Coder lifecycle events and policy responses'],
  ['Forge / Sentinel → Nexus', 'Ticket pair token', 'A2A verification tasks, progress, and results'],
  ['Runtime → GitHub', 'Brokered installation token', 'Repository API and Git operations'],
];
---

<DocsLayout breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Docs', href: '/docs' }, { label: 'Architecture', href: '/docs/architecture' }, { label: 'How the Pieces Talk' }]}>
  <h1>How the pieces talk</h1>
  <p>Manager owns privileged control-plane decisions. Nexus owns the tenant's agent workflow. Coder runs workspaces, and Redis stores tenant coordination state. The channel determines the credential and authority.</p>
  <DocsTable headers={['Channel', 'Authentication', 'What travels over it']} rows={CHANNELS} />
  <h2 id="runtime">Runtime API</h2>
  <p>Each workspace registers using a one-time bootstrap and receives an access/refresh pair. Manager derives its tenant, role, and repository from the workspace record. Nexus asks Manager to create workers; Manager records a durable operation and talks to Coder.</p>
  <h2 id="events">Hooks and A2A</h2>
  <p>Coder lifecycle events enter through Manager, which authenticates and routes them to the tenant's Nexus hook server. Agent CLI hooks run locally inside worker workspaces. Sentinel and Forge exchange verification tasks through Nexus's A2A relay, which persists evidence to tenant Redis.</p>
  <p>Read <a href="/docs/architecture/manager-runtime">Manager Runtime</a>, <a href="/docs/architecture/credentials">Credentials and Trust</a>, and <a href="/docs/architecture/hooks-and-a2a">Hooks and A2A</a> for the full request flows.</p>
</DocsLayout>
